Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 00:55:49 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] 10054: Preserve template namespaces before operator-> and
 operator->*

Keep template namespaces before a terminal operator-> or
 operator->*

The '>' in operator-> and operator->* leaves the template counter
unbalanced, so SymbolPathParser fell back to splitting on every "::",
including the ones inside template arguments. Treat both like the other
terminal angle operators.

AI-generated by Claude Code.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../src/main/java/ghidra/app/util/SymbolPathParser.java       | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Ghidra/Framework/SoftwareModeling/src/main/java/ghidra/app/util/SymbolPathParser.java b/Ghidra/Framework/SoftwareModeling/src/main/java/ghidra/app/util/SymbolPathParser.java
index 8d43ab3772..fbfd29dced 100644
--- a/Ghidra/Framework/SoftwareModeling/src/main/java/ghidra/app/util/SymbolPathParser.java
+++ b/Ghidra/Framework/SoftwareModeling/src/main/java/ghidra/app/util/SymbolPathParser.java
@@ -175,7 +175,9 @@ public class SymbolPathParser {
 			     "operator>>", 
 			     "operator<<=", 
 			     "operator>>=", 
-			     "operator<=>" -> true;
+			     "operator<=>",
+			     "operator->",
+			     "operator->*" -> true;
 			default -> false;
 		};
 		//@formatter:on
